 "_note": "FORM VALIDITY AGGREGATION and the SUBMIT GATE (U08 · <form> on:invalid / dirty / valid / submitting / disabled). RULE LAW: `required` is the only rule an EMPTY value can fail — every other rule passes on empty, so `validate=\"email\"` alone never blocks an untouched optional field; pair it with `required`. The rule vocabulary is required · email · url · phone · minLength:n · maxLength:n · pattern (the regex arrives in the sibling `pattern=` attribute so a ',' inside a quantifier cannot collide with the validate= separator). The FIRST failing rule owns the message; `message=` overrides it. AGGREGATION: form.valid is 'no registered field carries an error', form.dirty is 'some field differs from its initial value', and the on:invalid payload is the offending field names in REGISTRATION order. SUBMIT GATE (the double-submit law): a submit while `submitting` is already true, or while the form is `disabled`, is BLOCKED and runs nothing — that is the framework-level answer to a double-tapped order button; an invalid submit marks every field touched, sets form.submitted so every error reveals at once, and fires on:invalid; a valid submit sets submitting=true and runs on:submit. Expected values come from an independent scratch implementation.",
